cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "Madrid Housing Price Regression Benchmark"
authors:
  - family-names: Gamarra
    given-names: Francisco
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-14"
url: "https://github.com/franciscogamarra10/madrid-housing-regression-benchmark"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  Empirical comparison of custom feature pipelines, Skrub, AutoGluon and FLAML
  on Madrid residential listing prices. Shows that a compact FLAML DataTransformer
  plus default LightGBM outperforms AutoGluon best_quality on RMSE while being
  ~126× smaller and ~19× faster at inference.
keywords:
  - automl
  - feature-engineering
  - lightgbm
  - flaml
  - autogluon
  - tabular-ml
  - benchmark
  - housing-prices
